# The C++ examples of the website, the book, and the design notes compile,
# every function in them verifies unless the page says otherwise, and the
# verdicts a page shows are the ones the verifier gives.
# website/scripts/check-doc-examples.py describes the comments that mark
# fragments and expected failures.
# RUN: %python %S/../../../website/scripts/check-doc-examples.py \
# RUN:   --cpp-verify %cpp-verify %S/../../../website/source \
# RUN:   %S/../../../docs/DESIGN.md | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: examples checked ({{[0-9]+}} against the verdicts their pages show), 0 failed
